	Does anyone have any ideas about the following??

	I was in the dungeon when i came to a shop which was closed for
inventory, however my pet was sitting in the cell that had the message and
i didn't realise it was a shop. So i tried to open the door. It was locked.
I kicked the door in and got ...

As you kick the door it crashes open!
"Cad! you did 400 zorkmids worth of damage" Pay?

	I then hit the space bar (with hindsight it may have been the 'n'
key) and got...
"Oh yes you will pay!"
Manlobbi strikes at you displaced image and misses you!
Manlobbi strikes at you displaced image and misses you!
	At this point it seemed to be less than a good idea to be standing next
to manlobbi so I backed off. I thought i might try to pay again and see
if that calmed manlobbi. So I tried but forgot that there was now a space
between me and manlobbi. I got
Manlobbi is not near enough to recieve your payment.
	Ok I thought move closer - but Manlobbi moved away from me into the
shop. So i followed Manlobbi into the shop and to my suprise i get ...
"Hello, Turtledove! Welcome to Manlobbi's general store!"
	Moved farther into the shop and suddenly
Suddenly the shop door reappears!
	Tried to pay Manlobbi - but ...
You do not owe Manlobbi anything.
	The new door is unlocked and i can open it. Manlobbi is perfectly
friendly and was perfectly happy to sell me a pancake.

	At first I thought this was all a bug but the door appearing did
not seem like a bug. Maybe that is supposed to happen if you do pay the
shopkeeper and my unsuccesful attempt to pay him somehow satisfied him
even though it didn't reduce my stock of gold.

	This has really got me mystified.

